# Judge Hack — reference list of server-side environment names.
#
# THIS IS NOT A TEMPLATE. Do not copy it to `.env` and do not put a value in
# it. Judge Hack has no app-level `.env`: the app source reads no environment
# variables, and the build injects none. Every name below lives in RocketRide's
# own environment overlay, server-side, and is resolved there.
#
# The only real `.env` in this workspace is the developer's, at the repository
# root. The App Builder extension writes it, it is gitignored, and only the
# scripts in tools/ read it. It holds connection credentials, never app secrets.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORG scope — the app owner's credential, set once per instance by the owner
# in Account → Environment (org scope). Referenced from the generated .pipe
# files as ${ROCKETRIDE_ANTHROPIC_KEY} and substituted server-side, so the
# value never reaches the browser or the app bundle.
#
# Never write this from a script: account.setEnv replaces the entire dict at
# that scope and would delete everything else the org has.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROCKETRIDE_ANTHROPIC_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# USER scope — each judge's own GitHub personal access token, saved by that
# judge from Settings → GitHub access (which writes only their own user scope).
# Every GitHub read in a run uses it, so rate limits and repository access are
# theirs.
#
# Do NOT create this at org or team scope. The app only ever reads user scope,
# so one there is either dead weight or, if the read ever widened, a shared
# credential every judge would unknowingly run on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROCKETRIDE_GITHUB_TOKEN=   (per judge, never here, never org-wide)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform-injected, not ours: ROCKETRIDE_CLIENT_ID and ROCKETRIDE_DB_DSN are
# set by the engine inside its own pipeline processes so the cloud DB nodes
# resolve the right tenant database. Nothing a client sends can change them.
# When the engine is missing ROCKETRIDE_DB_BROKER_URL / _TOKEN, every store
# call fails with "ROCKETRIDE_CLIENT_ID is not set" — platform configuration,
# not an app defect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Personal Postgres placeholders were retired with hackjudge_sql_v1.external.pipe.
